<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Features | <%= project.title %></title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="page-shell">
      <section class="documentation-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Features</p>
        <h2>Program Pages and Features</h2>
        <p>
          This page explains the main screens in the inventory management program and what each one is used for.
        </p>
        <div class="link-row">
          <a class="button primary" href="<%= project.documentationUrl %>">Back to Documentation</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="<%= project.quickstartUrl %>">Quickstart Page</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="content-grid">
        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Login Page</h3>
          <p>
            The login page is the entry point for the program. It allows authorized users to sign in before accessing
            the inventory system. This supports the rule that only approved university users should be able to manage
            or view device records.
          </p>
          <figure class="screenshot-frame">
            <img src="/images/login.png" alt="Login screen for the inventory management system" />
            <figcaption>The login page used to verify users before they enter the system.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Dashboard</h3>
          <p>
            The dashboard is the main page of the program. It shows the inventory table, filter options, and the
            current list of devices. From this screen, users can review device details, check status information, and
            move into the add or edit workflows.
          </p>
          <figure class="screenshot-frame">
            <img src="/images/project-running.png" alt="Dashboard screen showing the inventory table and filters" />
            <figcaption>The main dashboard where users view and manage the equipment inventory.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Add Device Page</h3>
          <p>
            The add device page is used to create a new inventory record. Users can enter information for a new piece
            of equipment, such as its type, assignment details, and status, so it becomes part of the tracked device
            list.
          </p>
          <figure class="screenshot-frame">
            <img src="/images/add-device.png" alt="Add device form in the inventory management system" />
            <figcaption>The add device screen used to enter a new item into the system.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </article>

        <article class="info-card">
          <h3>Edit Device Page</h3>
          <p>
            The edit device page is used to update an existing inventory record. Users can change device details,
            assignments, or status values when equipment changes over time, which helps keep the inventory accurate.
          </p>
          <figure class="screenshot-frame">
            <img src="/images/edit-device.png" alt="Edit device form in the inventory management system" />
            <figcaption>The edit device screen used to update an existing inventory entry.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>